Source: adxl345
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Joseph Ambrose Pagaran <jagp.coin@proton.me>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cmake, pkg-config, libgpiod-dev (>= 2.0)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libadxl345-1
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: ADXL345 accelerometer library (runtime)
 A userspace driver for the ADXL345 over i2c-dev, with an opaque
 six-function C API, hidden visibility and a soname. It needs no kernel
 module: the part is driven entirely from user space.

Package: libadxl345-dev
Architecture: any
Section: libdevel
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libadxl345-1 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: ADXL345 accelerometer library (development files)
 The header and the pkg-config file, so a third party links the library
 the way any library is linked.

Package: adxl345-tools
Architecture: any
Depends: libadxl345-1 (>= ${source:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: ADXL345 reader and its udev rule
 adxl-map prints live acceleration. The package also ships the udev rule
 that puts /dev/i2c-* in group i2c, so that reading the sensor needs no
 root.
